+# Working with Rojo day to day
+
+Git is the source of truth for this game. Code lives in files under `src/`, and `rojo serve`
+syncs those files into your own dev place in Studio. The Layout table in [README.md](../README.md)
+shows where each folder ends up in the place.
+
+## First-time setup
+
+1. Install the tools: `rokit install`.
+2. Install packages: `pesde install` in the repo root, and again in `test_packages/`. This
+   creates `roblox_packages/` and `test_packages/roblox_packages/`. Both are generated and
+   ignored by Git.
+3. Make your own dev place: publish a fresh Baseplate to your own account or group. Never serve
+   into a shared, staging, or live place.
+4. Add your dev place's id to `servePlaceIds` in `default.project.json`, in a commit of its own.
+   Rojo then refuses to live-sync into any other place.
+5. Install the Rojo Studio plugin with the same version as the `rojo` in `rokit.toml`.
+
+## Daily loop
+
+1. `git pull`, then run `pesde install` (in the root and in `test_packages/`) if `pesde.toml` or
+   `pesde.lock` changed. Do this before you start `rojo serve`.
+2. Start `rojo serve` in the repo root. It listens on port 34872 (`servePort`).
+3. Open your dev place in Studio and click **Connect** in the Rojo plugin.
+4. Edit files in your editor. Rojo pushes each save into Studio.
+5. Before you push, run the checks in the README (`rojo sourcemap`, `luau-lsp analyze`, `selene`,
+   `stylua --check`). Run the Jest specs in Studio.
+6. Commit on your own branch and open a pull request.
+
+## Where changes go
+
+- **Make every change in files.** The dev place is a build of the repo. If you edit a script, add
+  an instance, or set a property or attribute under a synced folder in Studio, the next sync
+  overwrites it or Git never sees it, so it is lost.
+- Use the place to read, run, test, and playtest. If you try something in Studio, copy the change
+  into its file afterwards.
+- Put attributes and tags in a `Name.meta.json` (or `init.meta.json` in a folder), not in the
+  Properties window.
+- Never edit `roblox_packages/` or `test_packages/roblox_packages/`. They are replaced on every
+  install, and pesde hardlinks their files to a store that other projects share. Require packages
+  through their links, for example `require(ReplicatedStorage.Packages.Vide)`, and never through
+  a `.pesde/...` path.
+- Specs go in `src/ServerScriptService/Tests/Specs` as `Name.spec.luau`.
+- If a model or GUI has to be built in Studio, export it over its `.rbxm` file in the repo
+  (**Save to File**) and commit that file.
+
+## What to check while serving
+
+- **Rojo is still running.** Rojo 7.7.x can crash when a file or folder is deleted, moved, or
+  renamed. When that happens, Studio quietly stops getting changes. After you delete, move, or
+  rename something, look for `Rojo crashed!` in the terminal. If it crashed, restart `rojo serve`
+  and click Connect again.
+- **Your edit arrived.** Before you trust a test or playtest, open the script in Studio and check
+  that it has your new text. If an error points to a line number that didn't move after your edit,
+  Studio is still running the old code.
+- **The plugin shows no errors.** A protocol-version error means the plugin and `rojo` versions
+  differ.
+- **Stop `rojo serve` before big changes to the working tree:** `git checkout`, `switch`, `pull`,
+  `rebase`, `reset`, `stash`, `pesde install`, or deleting whole folders. Restart it afterwards.
+- **Know which branch you're serving.** The place runs whatever is checked out in the folder
+  where `rojo serve` started. Merging a pull request on GitHub changes nothing there until you
+  pull.
+
+## Keeping `default.project.json` healthy
+
+This file decides how the whole place is laid out. One bad merge can break the sourcemap, type
+checking, and Jest for everyone.
+
+- **The README's Layout table is the spec.** If you change a mount, update the table in the same
+  pull request.
+- **Resolve conflicts by hand against the Layout table.** Don't just pick one side. Common
+  mistakes:
+  - Typos in paths. `src/StarterPlayer/StarterPlayerScript` is not `.../StarterPlayerScripts`,
+    and Rojo won't warn you. The folder just ends up empty in the place.
+  - Moving the Jest packages. They must mount at `ServerScriptService.Tests.Packages`, because
+    specs and `jest.config` require them from there.
+  - Mounting `src/ServerScriptService/Tests` a second time. `ServerScriptService` already mounts
+    `src/ServerScriptService`, so `globIgnorePaths` keeps the `Tests` folder out of that mount,
+    and the project's `Tests` node builds it from `Specs` and `Packages`. If you remove either
+    part, `Tests` ends up duplicated or missing packages.
+- **Save it as UTF-8 without a BOM.** If the file starts with a byte order mark, Rojo fails with
+  `Failed to parse JSONC`. Windows PowerShell's `Set-Content` and `Out-File`, and some merge
+  tools, add a BOM. To check, run `head -c 3 default.project.json | od -An -tx1`. If it prints
+  `ef bb bf`, the file has a BOM and you need to remove it.
+- **Check it after every change or merge:**
+
+  ```sh
+  rojo sourcemap default.project.json -o sourcemap.json --include-non-scripts
+  luau-lsp analyze --platform=roblox --definitions:@roblox=globalTypes.d.luau --sourcemap=sourcemap.json --ignore=**/roblox_packages/** src
+  ```
+
+  Then look in Studio, or in `sourcemap.json`, and check that `ServerScriptService.Tests` holds
+  both `Specs` and `Packages` (with `Jest` and `JestGlobals`), and that `StarterPlayerScripts`
+  holds `Main`.
+- Ask for review on any pull request that touches `default.project.json`, even if it's a
+  one-line change.
